{
  "company_name": "FreshGuard Foods",
  "industry": "Food & Beverage",
  "use_case": "Quality event tracking and root cause analysis for food production",
  "space_title": "FreshGuard Foods - Quality Event Root Cause Analysis 🔍",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Food & Beverage\n\n**Use case:** Quality Event Tracking & Root Cause Analysis\n\nFreshGuard Foods — plant-level food safety and quality analytics across 20 SKUs and 12 production lines spanning bakery, dairy, deli, produce, protein, seafood, beverage, and frozen. Plant Managers and Quality VPs use this space day-to-day to investigate critical events, drill into root cause Pareto, and track CAPA closure; the VP of Food Safety and CFO use it to monitor audit readiness, non-conformance trends, and the cost of poor quality (COPQ) heading into FSSC 22000 / SQF surveillance audits.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Critical event count — zero-tolerance threshold; any critical NC can fail an SQF audit\n- Total cost impact ($) — COPQ rolled up by line, category, and root cause\n- Units affected per event — scale of containment / recall exposure\n- CAPA closure rate (%) — closed / (open + closed); target 90%+ on-time\n- Regulatory audit score — surveillance audit health vs. 85+ benchmark\n- Non-conformance count — monthly trend across compliance status\n- Pass rate on temperature compliance — cold-chain control indicator\n- Overall quality score — blended lot-release health 0–100\n\n**Data sources**\n- `product_lines` — daily quality events with severity, root cause, units affected, cost impact\n- `quality_events` — weekly inspections with microbe count, pH, temp compliance, disposition\n- `inspection_records` — monthly KPI rollup with CAPA open/closed, audit score, compliance status",
  "schema_basename": "fb_quality_rca",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "product_lines",
      "description": "Daily quality event records per product line with severity, root cause, and disposition.",
      "columns": [
