  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Quality Event Tracking & Root Cause Analysis for a multi-line food manufacturer regulated under FSMA, FSSC 22000, and SQF. Stakeholders include the Plant Manager (daily NCRs, line yield), the VP of Quality / Food Safety (audit readiness, CAPA velocity), and the CFO (cost of poor quality, recall exposure). Severity is Minor / Major / Critical; root causes follow a 6-bin Pareto (Equipment, Process, Ingredient, Contamination, Packaging, Handling).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Critical events = COUNT of product_lines.event_id WHERE severity='Critical'; target = 0 (any Critical NC can fail SQF audit)\n- COPQ = SUM(cost_impact_usd); benchmark 1-3% of revenue\n- Units affected = SUM(units_affected); a containment / recall scope proxy\n- CAPA closure rate = capa_closed / NULLIF(capa_open + capa_closed,0); target 90%+ on-time\n- Audit score = AVG(audit_score) from inspection_records; FSSC/SQF healthy ~85+\n- Non-conformance count = COUNT(kpi_id WHERE compliance_status='Non-Conformance')\n- Temperature compliance pass rate = pct of quality_events.temperature_compliance='Pass'\n- Overall quality score = AVG(overall_score) on quality_events; lot-release health 0-100\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - quality_kpi_monthly (source: product_lines) — dims: event_date, product_category, severity, root_cause; measures: total_events, total_units_affected, total_cost_impact, critical_events, avg_cost_per_event, unique_product_count, max_units_affected.\n  - inspection_kpi_monthly (source: inspection_records) — dims: kpi_month, product_category, production_line, compliance_status; measures: total_events_count, total_capa_open, total_capa_closed, avg_audit_score, nc_count, unique_product_count, max_events_count.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. product_id, product_name, microbe_count_cfu, ph_level, disposition).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show the monthly trend in critical events across all product categories for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 product categories by total cost impact this year — which root causes are driving the loss?",
    "Which production lines have the lowest average audit score, and how many non-conformances did they generate last quarter?",
    "How has total cost impact trended month-over-month across the network?",
    "Which root causes account for the highest share of critical events in the last 90 days?",
    "Top 10 product categories by units affected — show severity mix and total cost impact.",
    "What is the monthly trend in CAPA open vs. closed, and which production lines have the lowest closure rate?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique products?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(unique_product_count) AS unique_product_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.quality_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest units affected changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
